MODE="production"

# ─── The four off-box URLs, deliberately blank ────────────────────────────────
#
# These pointed at json.excalidraw.com, libraries.excalidraw.com and a Google
# Cloud Function until this change. Both halves of that are wrong for Lawha:
#
#   - With no internet — the normal state of the LAN this runs on — each one is
#     a DNS lookup that has to time out before the caller gives up. The user
#     sees a spinner, not an error, for as long as the resolver takes.
#   - WITH internet it is worse, because it works: `exportToBackend` ships a
#     whole scene, `PublishLibrary` ships every element you selected, to a
#     third party. A self-hosted, end-to-end encrypted canvas that posts its
#     contents to excalidraw.com is not self-hosted.
#
# Blank rather than removed, and rather than pointed at a local stub:
#
#   - REMOVING the lines does not help. `excalidraw-app/data/index.ts` reads
#     them at module scope and `packages/excalidraw` types them as `string`; an
#     absent key is `undefined`, which stringifies into the URL as the literal
#     "undefined" and produces a request to `/undefined<id>`. Blank at least
#     resolves against our own origin.
#   - A LOCAL STUB would be a lie: lawha-server has no shareable-link store and
#     no library registry, and inventing endpoints that always fail is more
#     code to explain than an empty value.
#   - The FEATURES' entry points stay. Removing "Export to shareable link" or
#     the library browse button means touching `packages/` (invariant 10) or
#     App.tsx, which is not this change. What they do now is fail locally and
#     immediately: `exportToBackend` already returns an errorMessage instead of
#     throwing, and `importFromBackend` already throws to a caller that reports
#     it — both were fixed when the window.alert sweep went through
#     (invariant 19). No network leaves the box either way, which is the point.
#
# If Lawha ever grows its own share-link store, these are the two lines that
# point at it, and they are already the only ones.
VITE_APP_BACKEND_V2_GET_URL=
VITE_APP_BACKEND_V2_POST_URL=

VITE_APP_LIBRARY_URL=
VITE_APP_LIBRARY_BACKEND=

# LEFT POINTING OFF-BOX, on purpose, and this is the one exception above.
#
# Nothing fetches these. They are `window.open` targets behind the Excalidraw+
# links in the command palette and sidebar — a user-initiated navigation to a
# marketing page, carrying no scene data — so there is nothing here to leak and
# nothing to hang on.
#
# VITE_APP_PLUS_APP additionally becomes `EXCALIDRAW_PLUS_ORIGIN` in
# excalidraw-app/ExcalidrawPlusIframeExport.tsx, where it is a postMessage
# targetOrigin. `postMessage(msg, "")` throws a SyntaxError, so blanking it
# would convert a dead route into a throwing one. Severing the Excalidraw+
# entry points means deleting them, which is a different change in files this
# one does not own.
VITE_APP_PLUS_LP=https://plus.excalidraw.com
VITE_APP_PLUS_APP=https://app.excalidraw.com


# Same origin. A production Lawha is served by lawha-server itself
# (LAWHA_STATIC_DIR) or by nginx in front of it, so the socket, the API and the
# app all share one origin — which is what keeps the session cookie first-party.
#
# This pointed at oss-collab.excalidraw.com until Phase 2: a production build
# would have collaborated through Excalidraw's hosted relay instead of the local
# one. Dev never noticed because .env.development already had it right.
VITE_APP_WS_SERVER_URL=/


VITE_APP_ENABLE_TRACKING=false

